@startuml 06-joueur
!include style.iuml
set separator none
title Le joueur — patterns State et Template Method

class Player <<focus>> {
  - state : PlayerState
  - skill1, skill2 : Skill
  - relics : List<Relic>
  + update(intent, world, dt)
  + strike(world) : int
  + receive(hit) : boolean
  + registerHit()
}

  interface PlayerState <<interface>> {
    + next(player, intent) : PlayerState
    + act(player, intent, world, dt)
    + invulnerable() : boolean
  }
  class IdleState
  class MovingState
  class AttackingState
  class DodgingState {
    invulnérable
  }
  class HurtState
  class DeadState

  abstract class Skill <<abstract>> {
    - cooldown, cooldownLeft : float
    + tryActivate(player, world) : boolean {leaf}
    # {abstract} activate(player, world)
  }
  class Shockwave {
    rayon 96 · 28 dégâts · étourdit
  }
  class BladeFan {
    7 lames · traversent 2 ennemis
  }

Player *-right- "1" PlayerState : état courant
Player *-down- "2" Skill
PlayerState <|.. IdleState
PlayerState <|.. MovingState
PlayerState <|.. AttackingState
PlayerState <|.. DodgingState
PlayerState <|.. HurtState
PlayerState <|.. DeadState
Skill <|-- Shockwave
Skill <|-- BladeFan

note right of PlayerState
  <b>State</b>
  Chaque état décide du suivant (next)
  et agit pendant le pas (act).
  Pas de grand switch dans Player.
  Les transitions : diagramme 07.
end note

note left of Skill
  <b>Template Method</b>
  tryActivate() est final : vérifier la recharge,
  appeler activate(), relancer la recharge.
  Une compétence n'écrit que son effet.
end note
!include legende.iuml
@enduml
